  </section>

  <section class="id-sources id-section" aria-labelledby="src-h2">
    <h2 id="src-h2">Sources</h2>
    <ol class="id-src-list">
      <li id="src-1">Heinrich, B. (1989). <em>Ravens in Winter</em>. Summit Books. — carcass recruitment, winter diet.</li>
      <li id="src-2">Madge, S. &amp; Burn, H. (1994). <em>Crows and Jays</em>. Christopher Helm. — diet breadth, plant material, prey types.</li>
      <li id="src-3">Boarman, W. I. &amp; Heinrich, B. (1999). Common Raven (<em>Corvus corax</em>). <em>The Birds of North America</em>, No. 476. — comprehensive diet data including human-associated foods.</li>
      <li id="src-4">Bugnyar, T. &amp; Heinrich, B. (2005). Ravens, <em>Corvus corax</em>, differentiate between knowledgeable and ignorant competitors. <em>Proceedings of the Royal Society B</em>, 272, 1641–1646.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="id-claim-note"><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> field-guide, species-account, and peer-reviewed data</p>
  </section>

  <nav class="id-nav-bottom">
